pull/23341
>=20
>=20
>=20
>=20
> I was also recently looking into https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFK=
A-20939 which was a blocker, too.
>=20
> Wondering if disabling KIP-909 behavior on the clients by default is suffi=
cient? -- Both Kafka Connect and Kafka Streams, expose all client config so u=
sers could enable this feature. I did look into both cases.
>=20
> For KS, it seems overall to be "safe", ie, nothing really bad would happen=
 if a user enables KIP-909, but there is also no benefit. The goal of KIP-90=
9 is to be more resilient against DNS changes, but KS would just crash with a=
n error and shut down hitting the new exception.
>=20
> However, for KC it seems to be problematic, as KC could enter a bad state i=
t cannot recover from, and it does not error out cleanly either. -- I am not=
 familiar with Connect and can only parrot what Claude spit out. Might be wo=
rth to double check by someone familiar with Connect?
>=20
> Maybe we should remove the new config from both KS and KC as quick fix for=
 4.4 release, and do proper follow-up work on each to make both KP-909 ready=
?
>=20
> Thoughts?
>=20
>=20
>=20
> -Matthias
