Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21084) Async consumer busy-loops when
 paused fetches are requeued into FetchBuffer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21084:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Async consumer busy-loops when paused fetches are req=
ueued into FetchBuffer
                 Key: KAFKA-21084
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21084
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


{*}Description{*}{*}{*}

AsyncKafkaConsumer.poll() can busy-loop when buffered fetches belong to pau=
sed partitions and no records can be returned. FetchCollector.collectFetch(=
) preserves paused fetches by requeuing them through FetchBuffer.addAll(). =
However, addAll() also sets=C2=A0wokenup =3D true. The subsequent awaitWake=
up() consumes this signal and returns without blocking.

=C2=A0

Repeated collection of the same paused fetches regenerates the signal, allo=
wing the application thread to spin in poll() until its=C2=A0timeout expire=
s, without new fetch responses or consumption progress.



