Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21089:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Ensure the producer gets closed in KafkaProducerTest =
to avoid cascading failures
                 Key: KAFKA-21089
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21089
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


from: [https://github.com/apache/kafka/actions/runs/34763157891/job/1037400=
45036?pr=3D23451]
{code:java}
Found 93 test failures:
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testCloseIsForcedOnPendingFindCoordina=
tor()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testSubscribingCustomMetricsWithSameNa=
meDoesntAffectProducerMetrics()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testRetriesAndIdempotenceForIdempotent=
Producers()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testCloseWhenWaitingForMetadataUpdate(=
)
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testTopicExpiryInMetadata()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > "testMetadataWithPartitionOutOfRange(b=
oolean).isIdempotenceEnabled=3Dtrue"
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > "testMetadataWithPartitionOutOfRange(b=
oolean).isIdempotenceEnabled=3Dfalse"
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > "testInitTransactionsWithKeepPreparedT=
xnAndTwoPhaseCommit(boolean, boolean).keepPreparedTxn=3Dtrue, enable2PC=3Df=
alse"
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > "testInitTransactionsWithKeepPreparedT=
xnAndTwoPhaseCommit(boolean, boolean).keepPreparedTxn=3Dtrue, enable2PC=3Dt=
rue"
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > "testInitTransactionsWithKeepPreparedT=
xnAndTwoPhaseCommit(boolean, boolean).keepPreparedTxn=3Dfalse, enable2PC=3D=
true"
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testDeliveryTimeoutAndLingerMsConfig()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testSendOffsetsToTransactionTriggersMe=
tadataRefreshThenNegotiatesV6()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testHeadersSuccess()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testTopicRefreshInMetadata()
FAILED =E2=9D=8C KafkaProducerTest > testNullGroupMetadataInSendOffsets() {=
code}
Many test cases in KafkaProducerTest don't close the producer in a try-with=
-resources or finally block. If an assertion fails in the middle of the tes=
t, the sender thread is leaked, and every subsequent test in the class fail=
s in {{detectLeaks}}=C2=A0

Also, the root cause of that failure is a too-small timeout (2000ms) for {{=
client.waitForRequests}}
{code:java}
client.waitForRequests(1, 2000); {code}



