Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21092:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: The closed processor should remove the channel builde=
r from reconfigurable list
                 Key: KAFKA-21092
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21092
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


{code:java}
=C2=A0 protected[network] def createSelector(channelBuilder: ChannelBuilder=
): KSelector =3D {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 channelBuilder match {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 case reconfigurable: Reconfigurable =3D> config.addRec=
onfigurable(reconfigurable)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 case _ =3D>
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 }
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 new KSelector(
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 maxRequestSize,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 connectionsMaxIdleMs,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 failedAuthenticationDelayMs,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 metrics,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 time,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "socket-server",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 metricTags,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 false,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 true,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 channelBuilder,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 memoryPool,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 logContext)
=C2=A0 } {code}
The processor lets Selector control the life of ChannelBuilder, but Selecto=
r can't remove the ChannelBuilder from the reconfigurable list. It is proba=
bly a kind of leak that the closed ChannelBuilder is still in the list.



