Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21097) Avoid duplicate share-partition
 next-fetch offset scans
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Shekhar Prasad Rajak (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-21097:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Avoid duplicate share-partition next-fetch offset sca=
ns
                 Key: KAFKA-21097
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21097
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: core
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak
            Assignee: Shekhar Prasad Rajak


Current flow :=C2=A0

=C2=A0DelayedShareFetch acquires the share-partition fetch lock, calls canA=
cquireRecords(), then calls nextFetchOffset() to build the log read.
=C2=A0 canAcquireRecords() already calls nextFetchOffset(), so a partition =
with released or timed-out records can scan cachedState and per-offset stat=
e twice
=C2=A0 under the write lock for one fetch.

=C2=A0

=C2=A0Proposed flow

=C2=A0 Add one atomic nextFetchOffsetIfAcquirable() call. Under one lock, i=
t computes the next fetch offset once and decides whether the partition can=
 fetch due
=C2=A0 to available redelivery records or remaining in-flight capacity. Del=
ayedShareFetch uses that returned offset directly.

=C2=A0 This removes the duplicate scan and lock gap without changing share-=
record state transitions or introducing a new availability index.

=C2=A0



