Hi,

Your project expressed interest in participating in the hackathon at
Community over Code Glasgow (October 11-14). We're finalizing the
schedule and we don't yet have a time slot claimed for your project.

We're now less than a month out from the event, and people are making
their decisions about whether to attend. The hackathon is one of the
things that draws contributors to Glasgow, and they're looking at the
schedule to see which projects will be there. An empty slot means
your community doesn't see a reason to show up.

The hackathon room is available Monday through Wednesday, and there
are still open slots =E2=80=94 especially on Wednesday. You can see the
current schedule and claim a slot by opening a PR:

  =
https://events.apache.org/events/2026/community-over-code/hackathon.html

If we don't hear from you by Friday September 19, we'll start
offering your slot to other projects that are waiting for space.

If your plans have changed and you're no longer able to participate,
just let us know =E2=80=94 no worries at all.

Thanks,
Rich=

