Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21100:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Defer to materialize the record body until it is conf=
irmed to be retained
                 Key: KAFKA-21100
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21100
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


This is similar to KAFKA-21082.=C2=A0

The other path, cleanInto / filterTo, could use a similar approach to defer=
 loading the value until we know the record must be retained.

The only fallback is when the oversized record is the newest value of its k=
ey and so must be kept. In this case, we could just keep the whole batch as=
-is (writeOriginalBatch already does this) to avoid reading the full value.=
 The side effect is that batch is not compacted, but it won't violate the c=
ompaction guarantee, since its key is already in the offset map and older v=
alues in other batches are still cleaned. The oversized record will be drop=
ped if it is not the newest one :)



