I don't think we have for 4.5... I believe that there was a slight, high 
level agreement for the long term, that we want to follow the "calendar 
week proposal"?

>>>>> KIP freeze would be Wednesday's, weeks 9 / 25 / 41, with feature freeze
>>>>> +3 weeks, and code freeze +2 weeks.

AK 4.4 KIP freeze was Jul/8.

For 2026, week 41 would be Oct/7 which is way too close IMHO.
For 2027, week 9 would be Mar/3 which seems to be too far out?

Second release (week 25) for 2027 would be Jun/23, which would be 4.6?

So the question remains, where to put 4.5 so we can start to follow the 
new schedule starting with 4.6. It seems KIP freeze between Jan 13 might 
be a good compromise putting it roughly between 4.4 and 4.6 KIP freeze 
dates. Of course, the release would overlap with Chinese New Year, but 
it would be the last time we have this overlap.

Just my 2tc.


-Matthias

