Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21110:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Document that min.insync.replicas is bounded by the r=
eplica count
                 Key: KAFKA-21110
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21110
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


{code:java}
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 public static final String MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_CONFIG =3D "m=
in.insync.replicas";
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 public static final String MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_DOC =3D "Spec=
ifies the <i>minimum</i> number of in-sync replicas (including the leader) =
" +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "required for a write to succeed when a produce=
r sets <code>acks</code> to \"all\" (or \"-1\"). In the <code>acks=3Dall</c=
ode> " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "case, every in-sync replica must acknowledge a=
 write for it to be considered successful. E.g., if a topic has " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<code>replication.factor</code> of 3 and the I=
SR set includes all three replicas, then all three replicas must acknowledg=
e an " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<code>acks=3Dall</code> write for it to succee=
d, even if <code>min.insync.replicas</code> happens to be less than 3. " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "If <code>acks=3Dall</code> and the current ISR=
 set contains fewer than <code>min.insync.replicas</code> members, then the=
 producer " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "will raise an exception (either <code>NotEnoug=
hReplicas</code> or <code>NotEnoughReplicasAfterAppend</code>).<br> " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "Regardless of the <code>acks</code> setting, t=
he messages will not be visible to the consumers until " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "they are replicated to all in-sync replicas an=
d the <code>min.insync.replicas</code> condition is met.<br> " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "When used together, <code>min.insync.replicas<=
/code> and <code>acks</code> allow you to enforce greater durability guaran=
tees. " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "A typical scenario would be to create a topic =
with a replication factor of 3, " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "set <code>min.insync.replicas</code> to 2, and=
 produce with <code>acks</code> of \"all\". " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "This ensures that a majority of replicas must =
persist a write before it's considered successful by the producer and it's =
visible to consumers." +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<p>Note that when the Eligible Leader Replicas=
 feature is enabled, the semantics of this config changes. Please refer to =
<a href=3D\"https://kafka.apache.org/documentation/#eligible_leader_replica=
s\">the ELR section</a> for more info.</p>";
 {code}
Since 3.7.0 (#14594, part of KIP-966), the broker uses {{min(min.insync.rep=
licas, replica count)}} as the effective min ISR. This applies to both {{ac=
ks=3Dall}} produce requests and the high watermark advancement, and it is n=
ot related to whether ELR is enabled.

The current doc does not mention this, and it still says the producer gets =
{{NotEnoughReplicas}} when the ISR is smaller than {{{}min.insync.replicas{=
}}}. The ELR note also implies the semantics change with ELR, but the ELR s=
ection only covers config management rules ...



--
