Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Chia-Ping Tsai (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21125:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Ensure the remote metrics get removed on leadership c=
hange
                 Key: KAFKA-21125
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21125
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


KAFKA-21098 and KAFKA-21124 add the guard to the methods that update the me=
trics. However, the guard is not 100% reliable since the race between the c=
heck and the update could still re-register the metrics.

A simple approach is that the tasks should remove their own metrics when th=
ey exit after being cancelled. The deletion is idempotent so we can tolerat=
e the duplicate delete operations =F0=9F=99=82



