Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21128:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: upgrade-guide.md could use more general version in de=
scribing upgrade path
                 Key: KAFKA-21128
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21128
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


=C2=A0
{code:java}
# Upgrade Guide and API ChangesUpgrading from any older version to 4.3.0 is=
 possible: if upgrading from 3.4 or below, you will need to do two rolling =
bounces, where during the first rolling bounce phase you set the config `up=
grade.from=3D"older version"` (possible values are `"2.4" - "3.4"`) and dur=
ing the second you remove it. This is required to safely handle 2 changes. =
The first is a change in foreign-key join serialization format. The second =
is a change in the serialization format for an internal repartition topic. =
For more details, please refer to [KIP-904](https://cwiki.apache.org/conflu=
ence/x/P5VbDg):=C2=A0=C2=A0 * prepare your application instances for a roll=
ing bounce and make sure that config `upgrade.from` is set to the version f=
rom which it is being upgrade.
=C2=A0 * bounce each instance of your application once=C2=A0
=C2=A0 * prepare your newly deployed 4.3.0 application instances for a seco=
nd round of rolling bounces; make sure to remove the value for config `upgr=
ade.from`
=C2=A0 * bounce each instance of your application once more to complete the=
 upgrade=C2=A0As an alternative, an offline upgrade is also possible. Upgra=
ding from any versions as old as 0.11.0.x to 4.3.0 in offline mode require =
the following steps:=C2=A0=C2=A0 * stop all old (e.g., 0.11.0.x) applicatio=
n instances=C2=A0
=C2=A0 * update your code and swap old code and jar file with new code and =
new jar file=C2=A0
=C2=A0 * restart all new (4.3.0) application instances=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 {code}
I think (and hope) this description applies to all 4.3+ versions. If yes, w=
e could replace "4.3.0" with "the current release". Otherwise, it looks lik=
e 4.4.0 has some issues during upgrade.



--
