Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21151) Extract streams group topology
 description orchestration into a shared runtime abstraction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Lucy Liu (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Lucy Liu created KAFKA-21151:
--------------------------------

             Summary: Extract streams group topology description orchestrat=
ion into a shared runtime abstraction
                 Key: KAFKA-21151
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21151
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Lucy Liu
            Assignee: Lucy Liu


The streams-group topology-description plugin's orchestration (push validat=
ion, the UNCERTAIN barrier write, plugin invocation and epoch bookkeeping, =
the periodic cleanup cycle, and the DeleteGroups pre-delete flow) is implem=
ented directly inside GroupCoordinatorService, with its logic tightly coupl=
ed to `CoordinatorRuntime<GroupCoordinatorShard, CoordinatorRecord>`

This split leaves related logic scattered between the two classes and keeps=
 `GroupCoordinatorService` doing state-machine-level work that belongs clos=
er to the component that already owns the plugin and back-off it's=C2=A0dri=
ving.

=C2=A0We should extract the read/write operations this orchestration needs =
against streams group state behind a narrow interface, and move the orchest=
ration itself out of `GroupCoordinatorService` and into `StreamsGroupTopolo=
gyDescriptionManager,` so all of the topology description plugin's logic, s=
tate, and orchestration live in one cohesive class



