Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21152) LogCompactionTester stops at the
 first empty poll and misses data after compaction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Eric Chang (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Eric Chang created KAFKA-21152:
----------------------------------

             Summary: LogCompactionTester stops at the first empty poll and misses data after compaction
                 Key: KAFKA-21152
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21152
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: system tests, tools
            Reporter: Eric Chang
            Assignee: Eric Chang
         Attachments: build948-trimmed.log

{{LogCompactionTest.test_log_compaction}} is flaky. {{LogCompactionTester.consumeMessages()}} stops when {{poll()}} returns no records:

{code:java}
if (consumerRecords.isEmpty()) return consumedFilePath;
{code}

Since KAFKA-12980 (3.2.0), an empty {{poll()}} does not mean the end of the log. After compaction, a batch keeps its {{lastOffset}} even when its last records are removed. If one {{poll()}} returns exactly {{max.poll.records}} records and the last one is the last live record of a fetch, the next {{poll()}} only moves the position to {{lastOffset + 1}} and returns no records right away. The tester then stops early and the validation fails.

In the 4.4.0-rc1 run (zstd level 10, ISOLATED_KRAFT), the tester read only 7498 of about 191k rows. It stopped at a batch with {{lastOffset}} 649433 whose last live record is 649426. The same case passed 5 out of 5 times on rerun. This is not a 4.4 regression and should not block the release: the consumer behavior exists since 3.2.0, and the tester code is even older. The trimmed logs are attached.

Simple repro (offsets 5..9 compacted away; {{fetch.max.bytes=1}} for one batch per fetch, {{max.poll.records=5}}):

{noformat}
poll#1 count=5 position=5  endOffset=16   (offsets 0..4)
poll#2 count=0 position=10 endOffset=16   (skips removed offsets 5..9: empty, but not at the end)
poll#3 count=5 position=15 endOffset=16   (offsets 10..14)
{noformat}

The consumer behavior is expected (KAFKA-14865 tracks it). This ticket only fixes the tester.

Fix: get the end offsets before consuming, and poll until the position of every partition reaches its end offset, with an overall timeout.




