{code:java}
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 public boolean isEmpty() {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 return records.isEmpty();
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 }
 {code}
The empty list will make {{ConsumerRecords#isEmpty}} return false, and {{pa=
rtitions()}} will include a partition with no records. I have checked that =
both classic and async consumers follow the rule. [https://github.com/apach=
e/kafka/pull/23532] will fix the issue in share consumer.

I was thinking of modifying {{{}isEmpty{}}}, but it may introduce an unexpe=
cted breaking change, and the constructor is public so interceptors can bui=
ld {{ConsumerRecords}} too. That is to say ... let's update the docs instea=
d =F0=9F=99=82



