Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21159)  Clear next offsets to consume on
 task close to avoid stale commit after revive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Bill Bejeck (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Bill Bejeck created KAFKA-21159:
-----------------------------------

             Summary:  Clear next offsets to consume on task close to avoid=
 stale commit after revive
                 Key: KAFKA-21159
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21159
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
            Reporter: Bill Bejeck
             Fix For: 4.5.0, 4.4.1


A revived active task (`closeDirtyAndRevive`) kept `nextOffsetsAndMetadataT=
oBeConsumed`
from before the corruption. After the consumer is seeked back to its commit=
ted offset, a
commit driven by processor metadata (`needsCommit`, which commits all input=
 partitions)
could fall back to that stale next offset and commit past records the task =
hasn't
reprocessed =E2=80=94 skipping them if the task later moves, and purging th=
em for a repartition
topic. The KAFKA-20416 `consumedOffsets.clear()` fix does not cover this pa=
th.

Fix: clear `nextOffsetsAndMetadataToBeConsumed` in `StreamTask.close()`, al=
ongside
`consumedOffsets`, so a revived task has no stale fallback for a partition =
it hasn't
re-read.



