Ziyun Fu created KAFKA-21166:
--------------------------------

             Summary: sticky assignor maybe never converge
                 Key: KAFKA-21166
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21166
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Ziyun Fu


While running the fuzz test with other base seeds to task sticky assignor, =
I found some cases where standbys never be stable.

If we take the output of {{{}assign(){}}}, feed it back as the members' cur=
rent assignment and call {{assign() }}again, some scenarios never reach a f=
ixed point, cause a few standby tasks land on member1, move to member2 in t=
he next round, come back to member1 in the round after that, and so on inde=
finitely.

Active tasks are not affected, only standbys.=C2=A0

If this keep happening, every time there's a rebalance, member1 and member2=
 will need to swap the standby and it's a extra cost for rebalance.



