Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21167) StickyTaskAssignor can overlook
 local state when a member reaches quota
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21167:
------------------------------------

             Summary: StickyTaskAssignor can overlook local state when a me=
mber reaches quota
                 Key: KAFKA-21167
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21167
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


The broker-side StickyTaskAssignor selects a previous-state candidate befor=
e checking its quota. A member at quota can prevent another eligible member=
 in the same process from being selected, causing unnecessary state restora=
tion.

=C2=A0
There are three stateful tasks and five members, giving an active task quot=
a of one per member: * Process P has two members: p1 previously owned task =
0, and p2 had no active tasks. Both report local state for task 2.
 * Process Q has three members: q1 previously owned task 1, while q2 and q3=
 had no active tasks. None report local state for task 2.

After tasks 0 and 1 are retained, p1 is at quota while p2 remains available=
. If p1 is considered first, p2 cannot replace it because both members have=
 the same process load. The subsequent quota check rejects p1 without tryin=
g p2.

Task 2 then falls back to load-based assignment, which selects Q because it=
s load is 1/3, compared with P's 1/2 even if p2 has local state for task 2.



