sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21169:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Streams group coordinator may trigger unnecessary reb=
alances on every heartbeat when a custom assignor returns empty task sets
                 Key: KAFKA-21169
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21169
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


Custom task assignors may use different representations for a subtopology w=
ith no assigned tasks. Some implementations omit the subtopology entry, whi=
le others include it with an empty task set:
=C2=A0
{code:java}
// No standby tasks: omit the subtopology entry.
Map.of()

// No standby tasks: include the subtopology with an empty set.
Map.of("subtopology-1", Set.of()){code}
Both representations assign zero standby tasks. The public MemberAssignment=
 API does not explicitly require empty subtopology entries to be omitted, a=
nd the coordinator accepts and persists them.

However, the target assignment preserves empty entries, while reconciliatio=
n omits them from the current assignment. TasksTuple.sameTasks() treats the=
se representations as different. As a result, an otherwise stable Streams g=
roup can trigger an unnecessary assignment refinement on every subsequent h=
eartbeat, even though its actual task assignment has not changed.

This advances the group, target assignment, and member epochs and generates=
 additional coordinator records. Reconciliation leaves the same representat=
ion difference in place, so the next heartbeat triggers another update.

Here, an unnecessary rebalance means an epoch and assignment update in the =
coordinator. In the reproduction, the assignor was called only once; the su=
bsequent updates did not require rerunning it. Task restarts or data loss h=
ave not been demonstrated.



--
