>
>
> combineStateBatches() merges batchesSoFar + newBatches into a sorted, dis=
joint, (deliveryState, deliveryCount)-distinct cover clipped at SPSO. Pipel=
ine:
> pruneBatches drops/clips ranges below SPSO.
> mergeBatches loads survivors into a TreeSet, repeatedly finds the first o=
verlapping or contiguous-same-state pair.
> Improvement area :
> =C2=A0iterative pairwise TreeSet merging. Simple contiguous same-state in=
put is roughly O(n log n), but overlap-heavy inputs can trigger repeated sp=
lit/reinsert rounds. The number of merge iterations is=C2=A0 data-dependent=
 and can grow non-linearly, approaching O(n^2 log n) in pathological overla=
p cases.
> =C2=A0
> User-visible as non-linear WriteShareGroupState latency when many small a=
ck ranges accumulate per partition.
> We can make it Time: O(n log n) (sort) + O ( n ) merge=20
> How:
> Replace the TreeSet + iterative findMergeCandidatePair loop with a single=
-pass sweep-line over a sorted array:
> 1. Sort phase (O(n log n)): prune + sort into ArrayList
> 2. Sweep phase (O( n )



