Luke Chen created KAFKA-21178:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Allow kafka admin to disable some compression methods
                 Key: KAFKA-21178
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21178
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Luke Chen


We've seen the snappy-java CVEs=C2=A0
 * CVE-2026-93452 ([snappy issue|https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/issu=
es/732])
 * CVE-2026-90559 ([snappy issue|https://github.com/xerial/snappy-java/issu=
es/728])

Unfortunately, the snappy-java community seems to be not maintained anymore=
.=C2=A0

Moreover, the is [lz4-jave community|https://github.com/lz4/lz4-java] is no=
t maintained anymore, either. Currently, we use the [forked repo|https://gi=
thub.com/yawkat/lz4-java] created by a user (yawkat). The single user repos=
itory might enter the unmaintained state anytime.

=C2=A0

proposal:

To improve that, we can create a config to allow kafka admin to disable som=
e compression methods when written. This way, we can avoid the bad users to=
 attack kafka using these impacted compression methods.

Note: we cannot get rid of these compression methods because the history lo=
g in kafka will not be able to be decompressed anymore.

=C2=A0

=C2=A0

=C2=A0



