Congrats Sushant, Well Deserved!

On Tue, Sep 29, 2026 at 2:20=E2=80=AFPM Apoorv Mittal <apoorvmittal10@gmail=
.com>
wrote:

> Congratulations Sushant, very well deserved!
>
> Regards,
> Apoorv Mittal
>
>
> On Tue, Sep 29, 2026 at 9:48=E2=80=AFAM Luke Chen <showuon@gmail.com> wro=
te:
>
> > Congratulations Sushant!
> >
> > Luke
> >
> > On Tue, Sep 29, 2026 at 5:45=E2=80=AFPM Sanskar Jhajharia via dev <
> > dev@kafka.apache.org> wrote:
> >
> > > Congratulations Sushant. Well deserved!
> > >
> > >
> > > On Tue, Sep 29, 2026 at 12:56=E2=80=AFPM Andrew Schofield <
> schofielaj@apache.org
> > >
> > > wrote:
> > >
> > > > The Project Management Committee (PMC) for Apache Kafka is pleased =
to
> > > > announce Sushant Mahajan as a new Kafka committer.
> > > >
> > > > Sushant has made several significant contributions to the project.
> > > > He built upon the work of the coordinator framework to introduce th=
e
> > > > share coordinator responsible for managing the state of share group=
s.
> > > > He created the batching and pruning mechanisms central to the share
> > > > coordinator's operation, balancing performance and resource usage
> while
> > > > ensuring data integrity. More recently, he added dead-letter queue
> > > support
> > > > for share groups.
> > > >
> > > > He shows great attention to detail and persistence in his
> > contributions,
> > > > and is a pleasure to work with.
> > > >
> > > > Please join me in welcoming and congratulating Sushant!
> > > >
> > > > Andrew Schofield
> > > > On behalf of the Apache Kafka PMC
> > > >
> > >
> >
