Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21182) StreamsGroupDescribe does not return
 tasks pending revocation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21182:
------------------------------------

             Summary: StreamsGroupDescribe does not return tasks pending re=
vocation
                 Key: KAFKA-21182
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21182
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


The Assignment field in StreamsGroupDescribe currently includes only assign=
edTasks, excluding tasks in tasksPendingRevocation. However, the coordinato=
r still considers the member responsible for these tasks until revocation i=
s acknowledged.

When an active task moves from member A to member B, it can therefore disap=
pear from both members=E2=80=99 current assignments in the Describe respons=
e: A is still pending revocation, while B cannot receive the task until A r=
eleases it. This makes it difficult to identify which member is holding up =
the transfer.

The same issue was fixed for consumer groups in KAFKA-20431. We should simi=
larly include tasks pending revocation in the assignment returned by Stream=
sGroupDescribe, covering active, standby, and warm-up tasks.



--
