sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21186:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Add test utilities for Streams custom assignors
                 Key: KAFKA-21186
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21186
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: streams
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Background*

KIP-1071 defines rules that Streams task assignments must satisfy. For exam=
ple, the same stateful task must not be assigned to different members shari=
ng the same processId, even in different roles such as active and standby.

With KIP-1357 enabling broker-side custom assignors, developers would benef=
it from an easy way to verify these rules in their unit tests. Shared test =
utilities would reduce the risk of developers overlooking or interpreting r=
ules differently when writing their own validation code.

=C2=A0

*Proposal*

Provide shared test utilities that custom assignor developers can use in th=
eir own tests.

Developers should be able to construct test inputs, run their assignor, and=
 pass the inputs and resulting assignment to the utilities to check complia=
nce with assignment rules. When a rule is violated, the utilities should id=
entify the affected tasks and members and explain the violation.

The checks should be based on KIP-1071=E2=80=99s requirements and aligned w=
ith the active and standby assignment responsibilities of custom assignors =
under the current public API. This would help developers test the constrain=
ts required by the Streams protocol while implementing their own assignment=
 policies.



--
