Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21187) OffsetCommit returns
 UNKNOWN_MEMBER_ID instead of FENCED_INSTANCE_ID for replaced classic static
 members in a ConsumerGroup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21187:
------------------------------------

             Summary: OffsetCommit returns UNKNOWN_MEMBER_ID instead of FEN=
CED_INSTANCE_ID for replaced classic static members in a ConsumerGroup
                 Key: KAFKA-21187
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21187
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Description*

ConsumerGroup.validateOffsetCommit() looks up the member by memberId withou=
t first validating the current owner of groupInstanceId.

When static member A is replaced by member B using the same instance ID, A=
=E2=80=99s member ID is removed. A subsequent non-transactional OffsetCommi=
t from A therefore receives UNKNOWN_MEMBER_ID instead of FENCED_INSTANCE_ID=
.

Under the same conditions, OffsetCommit in a ClassicGroup and classic Heart=
beat in a ConsumerGroup return FENCED_INSTANCE_ID.

*Impact*

Upon receiving UNKNOWN_MEMBER_ID from OffsetCommit, the classic client clea=
rs its member ID and requests to rejoin. A rejoin request with an empty mem=
ber ID and the same instance ID can replace the current static member B aga=
in.

Heartbeat fencing does not always prevent this. If the commit error resets =
the generation first, a delayed fencing heartbeat response for the previous=
 generation can be ignored as stale.

*Expected Behavior*

For replaced classic static members in a ConsumerGroup, OffsetCommit should=
 preserve the existing static membership fencing behavior and return FENCED=
_INSTANCE_ID.

=C2=A0

*NOTE*

{{ConsumerGroup.validateOffsetCommit()}} also handles members using the new=
 consumer protocol. The new client=E2=80=99s commit response handler has no=
 dedicated handling for {{{}FENCED_INSTANCE_ID{}}}, so any additional valid=
ation must consider compatibility with both protocols.



