Andrew Schofield resolved KAFKA-21041.
--------------------------------------
    Fix Version/s: 4.5.0
       Resolution: Fixed

> ClientMetricsConfigs rejects match patterns whose regex contains an equal=
s sign
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-21041
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21041
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>    Affects Versions: 4.3.1
>            Reporter: cuishuang
>            Priority: Trivial
>             Fix For: 4.5.0
>
>
> ClientMetricsConfigs.parseMatchingPatterns currently splits client match =
patterns using String.split("=3D"), which splits on every equals sign.
> The method Javadoc specifies that a client match pattern is split into tw=
o parts at the first occurrence of '=3D'.
> For example:
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 client_id=3Dfoo=3Dbar
> should be parsed as:
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 parameter: client_id
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 regex: =C2=A0 =C2=A0foo=3Dbar
> However, the current implementation produces three parts and throws Inval=
idConfigurationException.
> Expected behavior:
> The first '=3D' separates the parameter name from the regular expression,=
 and additional '=3D' characters remain part of the regular expression.
> Actual behavior:
> Patterns whose regular expression contains '=3D' are rejected.
> A fix using split("=3D", 2), together with a regression test, restores th=
e behavior described by the existing Javadoc.



