Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21188) Merging topics with different
 partition counts leaves some records unprocessed under the Streams
 Rebalance Protocol
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21188:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Merging topics with different partition counts leaves=
 some records unprocessed under the Streams Rebalance Protocol
                 Key: KAFKA-21188
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21188
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


With {*}group.protocol=3Dstreams{*}, merging two topics with different part=
ition counts includes nonexistent partitions in the tasks=E2=80=99 inputs, =
leaving some records unprocessed.

*Steps to Reproduce*

1. Create topic A with 1 partition({*}0{*}) and topic B with 3 partitions({=
*}0, 1, 2{*}).
2. Run the following topology with {*}group.protocol=3Dstreams{*}:
{code:java}
KStream<String, String> streamA =3D builder.stream("A");
KStream<String, String> streamB =3D builder.stream("B");

streamA.merge(streamB).to("output");
{code}
3. Produce records to {*}A-0{*}, {*}B-0{*}, {*}B-1{*}, and {*}B-2{*}.
 * *Expected:*=C2=A0All input records appear in `output`.
 * *Actual:*=C2=A0Records from `B-1` and `B-2` do not appear in `output`, a=
nd the following messages repeatedly reference nonexistent partitions:

{code:java}
Requesting the log end offset for A-1 in order to compute lag
Requesting the log end offset for A-2 in order to compute lag
{code}
=C2=A0

*Cause*

StreamsMembershipManager#topicPartitionsForActiveTasks and DefaultStreamsRe=
balanceListener#toTopicPartitions apply the task=E2=80=99s partition ID to =
every input topic without checking each topic=E2=80=99s partition count.

As a result, a task that should include only *B-1* also includes {*}A-1{*}.=
 The same issue occurs for partition ID 2.

The classic protocol=E2=80=99s PartitionGrouper checks each topic=E2=80=99s=
 partition count and includes only existing partitions. The new protocol=E2=
=80=99s conversion paths need equivalent handling.



