Dongnuo Lyu created KAFKA-21189:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Classic members in a consumer group are loaded with t=
he group level session timeout
                 Key: KAFKA-21189
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21189
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Dongnuo Lyu
            Assignee: Dongnuo Lyu


When a consumer group is reconstructed on coordinator load, `GroupMetadataM=
anager#onLoaded` schedules every member's session timer through `scheduleCo=
nsumerGroupSessionTimeout(groupId, memberId)`, which uses the group level `=
consumerGroupSessionTimeoutMs(groupId)`

=C2=A0

Members that joined with the classic protocol should use their own `session=
TimeoutMs` in `ConsumerGroupMemberMetadataValue.ClassicMemberMetadata`



